## Error cases

Run each case as a run, and as a dry run when the command has one. A dry run gives the code of the run for each case of the shared preparation. `exit-codes.md`, `error-codes.md`, and `wrap.md` of the contract fix these codes. `just contract` prints its folder.

| Case | Expected |
|---|---|
| A missing path, or a symbolic link to one | `USAGE_INVALID`, exit 2, and the message names the path |
| A symbolic link to the input | The answer for the file that the link names |
| `--timeout soon`, which is no duration | `USAGE_INVALID`, exit 2 |
| A `--timeout` that expires, such as `1s` on a long run | `RUNTIME`, exit 1, and the wrapped program stops |
| Ctrl-C during the run | `INTERRUPTED`, exit 130 |
| SIGTERM during the run | `TERMINATED`, exit 143 |
| An existing output without `--force` | `CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED`, exit 2, and the output does not change |
| A read-only output folder | `RUNTIME`, exit 1, before any effect |

Fill: the code of each case that `spec.md` decides, such as a command that refuses a symbolic link. The contract fixes no code for a link.

Fill: for a command that writes no file, such as the example, delete the two cases of the output.

Fill: each input that the wrapped program accepts but that the domain refuses, with its code, as `## Acceptance` in [spec.md](spec.md#acceptance) lists it.

## Uninstall

1. After the last run, run `just uninstall` in the clone.
2. Run `ncly describe {{ root }} --json`. It answers `NOT_FOUND`, exit 2.

Removal keeps the keys and the grants, as [Release and install](https://github.com/pascalandy/nicely/blob/main/docs/north-star/contract/extensions.md#release-and-install) says.

